IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lhl-dates`

-- Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018 (Vic) -- the rules.
--
-- Part 1 Division 2 (who provides labour hire services, who is a worker: ss 7 to 11) and the s 3 tiers; Part 2 (the
-- prohibitions: ss 13 to 16); Part 3 (who may apply, the declarations, grant and renewal, the licence period, objections,
-- annual information and fees, show cause, notifying changes, producing the licence); the Part 5 offences and duties a
-- provider, host or worker meets (ss 46, 67, 67A, 74, 79, 84 to 88, 91); Part 6 (civil penalties, the court, the time
-- limit, the bars of ss 97 and 98); Part 7 (VCAT review, s 102; prosecutions, s 105). The questions of the three seats are
-- in lhl-seat.l4 (the provider), lhl-seat-host.l4 (the host) and lhl-seat-worker.l4 (the worker), which import this module
-- and never restate a rule.
--
-- Answers follow the rulings on negatives (NOTES.md): JUST FALSE where the text itself says no, NOTHING (with a
-- NOTHING-kind tag) where it does not answer. What the Labour Hire Licensing Authority "is satisfied" of, "believes on
-- reasonable grounds" or "considers", what a host "reasonably believes", and a "reasonable excuse", are facts given to the
-- rules, never guessed. What the regulations prescribe (classes excluded by ss 10 and 11, circumstances in ss 7(3), 8(4),
-- 18(1), the renewal period of s 28(1), fees, prescribed changes) is not deposited and is asked as a fact.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL VERSION: quotations from a plain-text conversion by Legalese Commons of the Word file of the Labour Hire
-- Licensing Act 2018, Version No. 009 (1 October 2026), not the authorised version. (c) State of Victoria; published with
-- the authority of the Government Printer for the State of Victoria. No part may be reproduced except in accordance with
-- the Copyright Act 1968 (Cth). Quoted under the owner's ruling of 24 October 2026 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Labour Hire Licensing Act 2018`

GIVEN a IS A NUMBER, b IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the greater of` a `and` b MEANS IF a GREATER THAN b THEN a ELSE b

GIVEN `the first day` IS A DATE, `the second day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` `the first day` `and` `the second day` MEANS
    IF `the first day` `is before` `the second day` THEN `the second day` ELSE `the first day`

§§ `ss 7 to 11 -- providing labour hire services, and workers`

-- The kind of business the person conducts. s 7(1)(a) "in the course of conducting a business" (any business); s 8(1)(a)
-- "a business of providing recruitment or placement services"; s 8(2)(a) "a business of providing contractor management
-- services".
DECLARE `Kind of business` IS ONE OF
    `a business of providing recruitment or placement services`
    `a business of providing contractor management services`
    `another business`
    `no business`

-- The character of the arrangement with the other person (the host, s 7(4), 8(5)). s 7(1)(b) "the supply of labour";
-- s 8(1)(b), (2)(b) "the recruitment of individuals to supply labour for, or placement of the individuals with, another
-- person to perform labour for the other person". "Wholly or principally", directly or indirectly through another person.
DECLARE `Character of the arrangement` IS ONE OF
    `wholly or principally the supply of labour`
    `wholly or principally recruiting or placing individuals to perform labour for the other person`
    `something else`

-- The arrangement between the individuals who do the work and a provider (s 9).
DECLARE `How the individuals are engaged` IS ONE OF
    -- s 9(1): an arrangement under which the provider supplies, or may supply, the individual to other persons to perform
    -- work, and the provider is obliged to pay the individual (in whole or part), directly or through intermediaries.
    `a provider supplies them to others to perform work and must pay them for it`
    -- s 9(2)(a): the provider recruits the individual for, or places the individual with, other persons who are obliged
    -- to pay the individual.
    `a provider recruits or places them with others who must pay them for the work`
    -- s 9(2)(b): the provider recruits the individual as an independent contractor for other persons and manages the
    -- contract performance.
    `a provider recruits them as independent contractors for others and manages their contract performance`
    `none of these`

DECLARE `The arrangement` HAS
    `the kind of business`                                        IS A `Kind of business`
    `the character`                                               IS A `Character of the arrangement`
    `the engagement`                                              IS A `How the individuals are engaged`
    -- s 8(1)(d) "the provider also procures or provides accommodation for the individuals for some or all of the period"
    `accommodation is procured or provided for the individuals`   IS A BOOLEAN
    -- ss 7(3), 8(4) "the regulations may prescribe circumstances in which a person is taken to provide labour hire services"
    `the regulations take it to be labour hire services`          IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 10 (a) to (c): a prescribed class of provider, prescribed services, or a prescribed class of individuals supplied
    `the regulations exclude the provider, services or individuals` IS A BOOLEAN
    -- s 11: a prescribed class of individuals, or prescribed services provided by them
    `the regulations exclude the individuals as workers`          IS A BOOLEAN

-- s 9(1): "An individual is a worker, for a provider, if ..." with s 11 ("Despite section 9, an individual is not a worker
-- ... if"). An "if" definition: outside it, FALSE.
GIVEN `the engagement` IS A `How the individuals are engaged`, `excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(1) -- a worker` `the engagement` `excluded` IF
    (NOT `excluded`)
    AND CONSIDER `the engagement`
        WHEN `a provider supplies them to others to perform work and must pay them for it` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the engagement` IS A `How the individuals are engaged`, `excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(2)(a) -- a worker` `the engagement` `excluded` IF
    (NOT `excluded`)
    AND CONSIDER `the engagement`
        WHEN `a provider recruits or places them with others who must pay them for the work` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the engagement` IS A `How the individuals are engaged`, `excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 9(2)(b) -- a worker` `the engagement` `excluded` IF
    (NOT `excluded`)
    AND CONSIDER `the engagement`
        WHEN `a provider recruits them as independent contractors for others and manages their contract performance` THEN TRUE
        OTHERWISE FALSE

-- ss 9, 11: the individual is a worker for a provider under any head of s 9.
GIVEN `the engagement` IS A `How the individuals are engaged`, `excluded` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 9, 11 -- a worker for a provider` `the engagement` `excluded` IF
        `s 9(1) -- a worker` `the engagement` `excluded`
    OR  `s 9(2)(a) -- a worker` `the engagement` `excluded`
    OR  `s 9(2)(b) -- a worker` `the engagement` `excluded`

-- s 7(1): (a) in the course of conducting a business, an arrangement with another person; (b) the character is (wholly or
-- principally) the supply of labour; (c) the labour is performed by workers within s 9(1).
GIVEN a IS A `The arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 7(1) -- general labour hire` a IF
        (CONSIDER a's `the kind of business`
         WHEN `no business` THEN FALSE
         OTHERWISE TRUE)
    AND (CONSIDER a's `the character`
         WHEN `wholly or principally the supply of labour` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `s 9(1) -- a worker` (a's `the engagement`) (a's `the regulations exclude the individuals as workers`)

-- s 8(1): a recruitment or placement business, an arrangement whose character is recruiting or placing individuals,
-- workers within s 9(2)(a), and (d) the provider also procures or provides accommodation for them.
GIVEN a IS A `The arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(1) -- recruitment or placement with accommodation` a IF
        (CONSIDER a's `the kind of business`
         WHEN `a business of providing recruitment or placement services` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND (CONSIDER a's `the character`
         WHEN `wholly or principally recruiting or placing individuals to perform labour for the other person` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `s 9(2)(a) -- a worker` (a's `the engagement`) (a's `the regulations exclude the individuals as workers`)
    AND a's `accommodation is procured or provided for the individuals`

-- s 8(2): a contractor management business, an arrangement whose character is recruiting or placing individuals, and
-- workers within s 9(2)(b).
GIVEN a IS A `The arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 8(2) -- contractor management` a IF
        (CONSIDER a's `the kind of business`
         WHEN `a business of providing contractor management services` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND (CONSIDER a's `the character`
         WHEN `wholly or principally recruiting or placing individuals to perform labour for the other person` THEN TRUE
         OTHERWISE FALSE)
    AND `s 9(2)(b) -- a worker` (a's `the engagement`) (a's `the regulations exclude the individuals as workers`)

-- s 3 "provides labour hire services has the meaning given by section 7(1) and section 8(1) and (2)", with the prescribed
-- circumstances of ss 7(3), 8(4), and s 10 ("Despite sections 7 and 8, a person does not provide labour hire services ...
-- if"). A closed definition: outside it, FALSE.
GIVEN a IS A `The arrangement`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 7 to 10 -- provides labour hire services` a IF
    (NOT a's `the regulations exclude the provider, services or individuals`)
    AND (    `s 7(1) -- general labour hire` a
         OR  `s 8(1) -- recruitment or placement with accommodation` a
         OR  `s 8(2) -- contractor management` a
         OR  a's `the regulations take it to be labour hire services`)

§§ `s 3 -- tier 1, 2 and 3 businesses`

DECLARE `Tier` IS ONE OF
    `a tier 1 business (turnover of no more than $2 000 000)`
    `a tier 2 business (turnover of $2 000 001 to $10 000 000)`
    `a tier 3 business (turnover of more than $10 000 000)`
    `none of the three tiers: the turnover falls between the Act's ranges (more than $2 000 000 but less than $2 000 001)`

-- s 3, tier 1, 2 and 3 business, each a "means" definition: paragraph (a) on the turnover of the 4 quarters before the day
-- the turnover information is due, paragraph (b) on the projected turnover of the first 4 quarters for a business that did
-- not operate in those 4 quarters. Both paragraphs use the same figures, so the turnover asked is whichever applies. The
-- Act's figures are used; the regulations may prescribe others (not deposited). The ranges leave a gap of one dollar
-- (finding 2): a turnover of, say, $2 000 000.50 is in no tier.
GIVEN `the turnover` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Tier`
`s 3 -- the tier of the business` `the turnover` MEANS
    IF `the turnover` AT MOST 2000000
    THEN `a tier 1 business (turnover of no more than $2 000 000)`
    ELSE IF `the turnover` LESS THAN 2000001
         THEN `none of the three tiers: the turnover falls between the Act's ranges (more than $2 000 000 but less than $2 000 001)`
         ELSE IF `the turnover` AT MOST 10000000
              THEN `a tier 2 business (turnover of $2 000 001 to $10 000 000)`
              ELSE `a tier 3 business (turnover of more than $10 000 000)`

§§ `ss 26, 28, 39, 40 -- is the licence in force`

DECLARE `The licence` HAS
    `there is a licence`                                IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day it came into force`                        IS A DATE
    `the expiry date`                                   IS A DATE
    `it has been cancelled`                             IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the cancellation took effect`              IS A DATE
    `it is suspended on the day`                        IS A BOOLEAN
    `a renewal application was made`                    IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day the renewal application was made`          IS A DATE
    `it was made in the prescribed period`              IS A BOOLEAN
    `the renewal application has been decided or withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day it was decided or withdrawn`               IS A DATE

-- s 26: a licence "comes into force on the day specified" and "remains in force (i) until the date (the expiry date)
-- specified"; read with s 28(4) ("taken ... to have been in force from the expiry date"), the expiry date is the first day it
-- is not in force (fork F2). s 28(3): a renewal application made "before the expiry date" keeps it in force until it is
-- renewed, withdrawn or refused; s 28(4): one made "after the expiry date" deems it in force from the expiry date until then.
-- An application made on the expiry date itself is neither before nor after it (finding 3): from that day the answer is
-- NOTHING. A late application deems the licence in force back to the expiry date, days before it was made included (fork
-- F3). s 39(3): "A licence is not in force during a period of suspension". s 40(2)(b): cancellation takes effect on the
-- date stated.
GIVEN l IS A `The licence`, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`the licence is in force on` l `the day` MEANS
    IF NOT l's `there is a licence`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE IF `the day` `is before` (l's `the day it came into force`)
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF l's `it is suspended on the day`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE IF l's `it has been cancelled` AND (l's `the day the cancellation took effect` `is on or before` `the day`)
                   THEN JUST FALSE
                   ELSE IF `the day` `is before` (l's `the expiry date`)
                        THEN JUST TRUE
                        ELSE `kept in force by a renewal application`
    WHERE
        `the application is pending on the day` MEANS
                l's `a renewal application was made`
            AND l's `it was made in the prescribed period`
            AND (NOT (l's `the renewal application has been decided or withdrawn` AND (l's `the day it was decided or withdrawn` `is on or before` `the day`)))
        `kept in force by a renewal application` MEANS
            IF NOT `the application is pending on the day`
            THEN JUST FALSE
            ELSE IF l's `the day the renewal application was made` `is before` (l's `the expiry date`)
                 THEN JUST TRUE
                 ELSE IF l's `the expiry date` `is before` (l's `the day the renewal application was made`)
                      THEN JUST TRUE -- s 28(4): once made, the licence "is taken ... to have been in force from the expiry date", the gap included (fork F3)
                      ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: an application made on the expiry date is neither "before" (s 28(3)) nor "after" (s 28(4)) it; finding 3)

-- s 26(b)(i): the expiry date "must not be later than 3 years after the day on which the licence came into force"; s
-- 29(7)(b)(i): a renewed licence's period "must not be longer than 3 years beginning on the expiry date of the licence". The
-- last day either can be in force: the day before the third anniversary (of the first day in force, or of the old expiry
-- date) (fork F2).
GIVEN `the day counted from` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`ss 26, 29(7) -- the last day the licence can be in force` `the day counted from` MEANS
    `the date` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` (`the date` 3 `years after` `the day counted from`)

§§ `Part 2 -- the prohibitions`

-- s 13: "A person must not provide labour hire services unless the person is the holder of a licence that is in force."
-- Not providing labour hire services: the prohibition does not reach the person (NOTHING). Providing them with a licence in
-- force: the "unless" is met (JUST FALSE).
GIVEN `provides labour hire services` IS A BOOLEAN, `the licence is in force` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 13 -- providing labour hire services without a licence` `provides labour hire services` `the licence is in force` MEANS
    IF NOT `provides labour hire services`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 13 forbids only providing labour hire services)
    ELSE CONSIDER `the licence is in force`
         WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (NOT b)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: whether the licence is in force is not answered; see s 28)

-- s 14: "A person must not advertise or in any way hold out that the person provides, or is willing to provide, labour hire
-- services unless the person is the holder of a licence that is in force."
GIVEN `the licence is in force` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14 -- advertising labour hire services is forbidden` `the licence is in force` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the licence is in force`
    WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (NOT b)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: whether the licence is in force is not answered; see s 28)

-- s 15(1): "A person must not enter into an arrangement (directly or indirectly) for the provision of labour hire services
-- unless the proposed provider of the labour hire services is the holder of a licence that is in force." (2) "Subsection
-- (1) does not apply if (a) the provider was included in the Register as the holder of a licence at the time the
-- arrangement was entered into; or (b) the person otherwise has a reasonable excuse".
GIVEN `it is for labour hire services`       IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider holds a licence in force` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provider was on the Register`      IS A BOOLEAN
      `I have a reasonable excuse`            IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 -- entering the arrangement is forbidden` `it is for labour hire services` `the provider holds a licence in force` `the provider was on the Register` `I have a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    IF NOT `it is for labour hire services`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 15(1) forbids only arrangements for the provision of labour hire services)
    ELSE IF `the provider holds a licence in force`
         THEN JUST FALSE
         ELSE IF `the provider was on the Register` OR `I have a reasonable excuse`
              THEN JUST FALSE
              ELSE JUST TRUE

-- s 16(1): "This section applies if (a) a person (the client) proposes to enter into an arrangement with another person (the
-- supplier) for the supply of an individual to perform work ...; and (b) the supplier is not included in the Register as the
-- holder of a licence that is in force at the time the arrangement is proposed."
GIVEN `it is for the supply of an individual to perform work` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the supplier is on the Register with a licence in force` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 16(1) -- the section applies` `it is for the supply of an individual to perform work` `the supplier is on the Register with a licence in force` IF
    `it is for the supply of an individual to perform work` AND (NOT `the supplier is on the Register with a licence in force`)

-- s 16(2): "The client must not enter into the proposed arrangement if the client knows, or has reasonable grounds to
-- suspect, that the proposed arrangement is for the purpose of avoiding or circumventing an obligation ... by this Act."
-- Where s 16 does not apply, or the client neither knows nor has reasonable grounds to suspect: the "if" fails (JUST FALSE).
GIVEN `the section applies`                IS A BOOLEAN
      `I know or have reasonable grounds to suspect it is for avoidance` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16(2) -- entering the avoidance arrangement is forbidden` `the section applies` `I know or have reasonable grounds to suspect it is for avoidance` MEANS
    JUST (`the section applies` AND `I know or have reasonable grounds to suspect it is for avoidance`)

-- s 95: "(1) A person must not (a) aid, abet, counsel or procure a contravention of a civil penalty provision; or (b) induce
-- ... ; or (c) be in any way directly or indirectly knowingly concerned in, or party to, a contravention ...; or (d) conspire
-- to contravene a civil penalty provision. (2) This Act applies to a person who contravenes subsection (1) ... as if the
-- person had contravened the provision."
DECLARE `How I was involved` IS ONE OF
    `I aided, abetted, counselled or procured it`
    `I induced it, by threats, promises or otherwise`
    `I was knowingly concerned in it or party to it, directly or indirectly`
    `I conspired with others to contravene it`
    `I was not involved in any of these ways`

GIVEN `the involvement` IS A `How I was involved`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 95 -- treated as having contravened the provision` `the involvement` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the involvement`
    WHEN `I was not involved in any of these ways` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 95 reaches only the four kinds of involvement it lists)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Part 3 -- applications, grant and renewal`

-- s 18(1): "A person must not make an application under section 17 for a licence or under section 28 for renewal of a
-- licence if (a) within the preceding 2 years, a licence (however described) held by the person under a labour hire industry
-- law was cancelled other than (i) on the initiative of the person; or (ii) in the prescribed circumstances; or (b) ... the
-- prior application was refused, or a decision to refuse the prior application was upheld on review or appeal, other than
-- in the prescribed circumstances, during the period of 3 months immediately preceding the proposed application". The bar
-- runs to the day before the second anniversary of the cancellation, or the day before the day 3 months after the refusal
-- (fork F4). Only a cancellation or refusal on or before the proposed day is "preceding" it.
DECLARE `The history` HAS
    `a licence of mine was cancelled`                   IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day it was cancelled`                          IS A DATE
    `it was cancelled on my initiative`                 IS A BOOLEAN
    `the cancellation was in prescribed circumstances`  IS A BOOLEAN
    `a prior application of mine was refused`           IS A BOOLEAN
    `the day it was refused or the refusal upheld`      IS A DATE
    `the refusal was in prescribed circumstances`       IS A BOOLEAN

GIVEN h IS A `The history`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(1)(a) -- a cancellation counts` h IF
    h's `a licence of mine was cancelled` AND (NOT h's `it was cancelled on my initiative`) AND (NOT h's `the cancellation was in prescribed circumstances`)

GIVEN h IS A `The history`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18(1)(b) -- a refusal counts` h IF
    h's `a prior application of mine was refused` AND (NOT h's `the refusal was in prescribed circumstances`)

-- The first day the bar no longer stands: the second anniversary of the cancellation, or 3 months after the refusal.
GIVEN h IS A `The history`, `the proposed day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 18 -- the first day I may apply` h `the proposed day` MEANS
    `the later of` (`the later of` `the proposed day` `and` `after the cancellation`) `and` `after the refusal`
    WHERE
        `after the cancellation` MEANS
            IF `s 18(1)(a) -- a cancellation counts` h AND (h's `the day it was cancelled` `is on or before` `the proposed day`)
            THEN `the date` 2 `years after` (h's `the day it was cancelled`)
            ELSE `the proposed day`
        `after the refusal` MEANS
            IF `s 18(1)(b) -- a refusal counts` h AND (h's `the day it was refused or the refusal upheld` `is on or before` `the proposed day`)
            THEN `the date` 3 `months after` (h's `the day it was refused or the refusal upheld`)
            ELSE `the proposed day`

GIVEN h IS A `The history`, `the proposed day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 18 -- I must not apply` h `the proposed day` IF
    `the proposed day` `is before` (`s 18 -- the first day I may apply` h `the proposed day`)

-- ss 17(4), (5), (5A), 23, 28(2), 29(1): what must go with an application.
DECLARE `Kind of application` IS ONE OF
    `an application for a licence (s 17)`
    `an application to renew a licence (s 28)`

DECLARE `What must go with it` IS ONE OF
    `a declaration that each relevant person is a fit and proper person (s 17(4)(a))`
    `a declaration that the applicant is financially viable (ss 17(4)(ab), 29(1)(da))`
    `a declaration of compliance with the laws in s 23(1A) (s 17(4)(b))`
    `a declaration that the applicant has complied, is complying and will continue to comply with the laws in s 23(1A) (s 23(1))`
    `a declaration that the applicant has a plan to comply with the laws in s 23(2) and can give it on request (s 23(2))`
    `a declaration that the accommodation will meet all applicable minimum accommodation standards (s 23(3)(a))`
    `a declaration that the transport will comply with all applicable transport laws (s 23(3)(b))`
    `a declaration that the applicant made reasonable inquiries about the application and declarations (s 23(4))`
    `a declaration that the information in the application is true and correct (s 17(4)(c), (d))`
    `the consent of each relevant person to the Authority getting information from third parties (s 17(5))`
    `an acknowledgement that the Authority may require further information under s 21 or 47 (s 17(5A))`
    `an acknowledgement that the Authority may require further information under s 31 or 47 (s 28(2)(d))`
    `the prescribed declarations, consents and acknowledgements (s 29(1)(c))`

GIVEN `the kind`                                IS A `Kind of application`
      `I am conducting a labour hire business`  IS A BOOLEAN
      `accommodation is procured for workers`   IS A BOOLEAN
      `transport is procured for workers`       IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A LIST OF `What must go with it`
`ss 17, 23, 28, 29 -- what must go with the application` `the kind` `I am conducting a labour hire business` `accommodation is procured for workers` `transport is procured for workers` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind`
    WHEN `an application for a licence (s 17)` THEN
        concat (LIST `the new application list`, `the s 23(3) list`, `the s 23(4) list`)
    WHEN `an application to renew a licence (s 28)` THEN
        concat (LIST `the renewal list`, `the s 23(3) list`, `the s 23(4) list`)
    WHERE
        `the new application list` MEANS
            LIST `a declaration that each relevant person is a fit and proper person (s 17(4)(a))`,
                 `a declaration that the applicant is financially viable (ss 17(4)(ab), 29(1)(da))`,
                 `a declaration of compliance with the laws in s 23(1A) (s 17(4)(b))`,
                 IF `I am conducting a labour hire business`
                 THEN `a declaration that the applicant has complied, is complying and will continue to comply with the laws in s 23(1A) (s 23(1))`
                 ELSE `a declaration that the applicant has a plan to comply with the laws in s 23(2) and can give it on request (s 23(2))`,
                 `a declaration that the information in the application is true and correct (s 17(4)(c), (d))`,
                 `the consent of each relevant person to the Authority getting information from third parties (s 17(5))`,
                 `an acknowledgement that the Authority may require further information under s 21 or 47 (s 17(5A))`
        -- s 23(2) speaks only of "an application for a licence"; a renewing holder not conducting a business gets no s 23
        -- compliance declaration (fork F5).
        `the renewal list` MEANS
            IF `I am conducting a labour hire business`
            THEN LIST `the prescribed declarations, consents and acknowledgements (s 29(1)(c))`,
                      `a declaration that the applicant is financially viable (ss 17(4)(ab), 29(1)(da))`,
                      `an acknowledgement that the Authority may require further information under s 31 or 47 (s 28(2)(d))`,
                      `a declaration that the applicant has complied, is complying and will continue to comply with the laws in s 23(1A) (s 23(1))`
            ELSE LIST `the prescribed declarations, consents and acknowledgements (s 29(1)(c))`,
                      `a declaration that the applicant is financially viable (ss 17(4)(ab), 29(1)(da))`,
                      `an acknowledgement that the Authority may require further information under s 31 or 47 (s 28(2)(d))`
        `the s 23(4) list` MEANS LIST `a declaration that the applicant made reasonable inquiries about the application and declarations (s 23(4))`
        `the s 23(3) list` MEANS
            IF `accommodation is procured for workers`
            THEN IF `transport is procured for workers`
                 THEN LIST `a declaration that the accommodation will meet all applicable minimum accommodation standards (s 23(3)(a))`, `a declaration that the transport will comply with all applicable transport laws (s 23(3)(b))`
                 ELSE LIST `a declaration that the accommodation will meet all applicable minimum accommodation standards (s 23(3)(a))`
            ELSE IF `transport is procured for workers`
                 THEN LIST `a declaration that the transport will comply with all applicable transport laws (s 23(3)(b))`
                 ELSE EMPTY

-- ss 24, 29 (1) to (3), with s 32(4)(a). The Authority's satisfactions and decisions are facts.
DECLARE `The application as decided` HAS
    `it includes the required information`               IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(1)(a) (s 17(2), (3)); s 29(1)(a)
    `it has the required declarations, consents and acknowledgements` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(1)(b) (s 17(4), (5)); s 29(1)(c), (da), (db)
    `the applicant was not barred by s 18`               IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(1)(c); s 29(1)(b)
    `the prescribed fee was paid`                        IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(1)(d); s 29(1)(d)
    `satisfied each relevant person is fit and proper`   IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(1)(e); s 29(1)(e)
    `satisfied each relevant person complies`            IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(1)(f); s 29(1)(f)
    `further information required was given to its satisfaction` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(1)(g); s 29(1)(g) (TRUE if none required)
    `satisfied the applicant is financially viable`      IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(1)(h); s 29(1)(h)
    `satisfied it is appropriate in all the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 24(2); s 29(2)
    `an objection was made`                              IS A BOOLEAN -- s 32(1)
    `the objection and response have been taken into account` IS A BOOLEAN -- s 32(4)(a)

DECLARE `What the Authority must do` IS ONE OF
    `it must grant or renew the licence (s 24(1), s 29(1))`
    `it may grant or renew the licence, being satisfied that is appropriate in all the circumstances (s 24(2), s 29(2))`
    `it must refuse to grant or renew the licence (s 24(3), s 29(3))`
    `it must not grant or renew yet: it must first take into account the objection and your response (s 32(4)(a))`

GIVEN a IS A `The application as decided`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `ss 24(1), 29(1) -- every condition is met` a IF
        a's `it includes the required information`
    AND a's `it has the required declarations, consents and acknowledgements`
    AND a's `the applicant was not barred by s 18`
    AND a's `the prescribed fee was paid`
    AND a's `satisfied each relevant person is fit and proper`
    AND a's `satisfied each relevant person complies`
    AND a's `further information required was given to its satisfaction`
    AND a's `satisfied the applicant is financially viable`

GIVEN a IS A `The application as decided`
GIVETH A `What the Authority must do`
`ss 24, 29, 32(4) -- what the Authority must do` a MEANS
    IF a's `an objection was made` AND (NOT a's `the objection and response have been taken into account`)
    THEN `it must not grant or renew yet: it must first take into account the objection and your response (s 32(4)(a))`
    ELSE IF `ss 24(1), 29(1) -- every condition is met` a
         THEN `it must grant or renew the licence (s 24(1), s 29(1))`
         ELSE IF a's `satisfied it is appropriate in all the circumstances`
              THEN `it may grant or renew the licence, being satisfied that is appropriate in all the circumstances (s 24(2), s 29(2))`
              ELSE `it must refuse to grant or renew the licence (s 24(3), s 29(3))`

§§ `Part 3 -- dates the holder meets`

-- s 34(3)(a), (5)(a), (b): the information "must be provided within 28 days of the start of the reporting period"; the first
-- reporting period is "the period of 12 months beginning on the day on which the licence first came into force", then "each
-- subsequent 12-month period". Reporting period n starts 12 x (n - 1) months after the first day; the last day for the
-- information is 28 days after its start (fork F6). A prescribed other period (s 34(5)(c)) is not deposited.
GIVEN `the first day in force` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 34(5) -- the start of reporting period` `the first day in force` n MEANS
    `the date` (12 TIMES (n MINUS 1)) `months after` `the first day in force`

GIVEN `the first day in force` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 34(3) -- the last day for the annual information` `the first day in force` n MEANS
    `the date` 28 `days after` (`s 34(5) -- the start of reporting period` `the first day in force` n)

-- s 35(1)(a): the annual fee is due "on the date the licence was specified to come into force ... or specified to be renewed
-- ... and on each subsequent anniversary"; s 35(2): it "may be paid at any time during the 6 weeks before it falls due". The
-- next due date on or after a day; an anniversary of 29 February falls on 28 February (fork F1). A prescribed other date
-- (s 35(1)(b)) is not deposited.
GIVEN `the date specified` IS A DATE, `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 35(1) -- the next day the annual fee falls due` `the date specified` `the day` MEANS
    IF `the day` `is on or before` `the date specified`
    THEN `the date specified`
    ELSE IF `the day` `is on or before` `this year's anniversary`
         THEN `this year's anniversary`
         ELSE `the date` (`the years` PLUS 1) `years after` `the date specified`
    WHERE
        `the years` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the day` MINUS DATE_YEAR `the date specified`
        `this year's anniversary` MEANS `the date` `the years` `years after` `the date specified`

GIVEN `the due date` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 35(2) -- the first day the fee may be paid early` `the due date` MEANS `the date` (0 MINUS 42) `days after` `the due date`

-- s 32(3)(b): the Authority must "allow a period of 14 days from the date of forwarding the notice for the applicant to
-- respond to the notice of objection". s 42(2)(c): the holder "may, within 14 days after the notice is given, give the
-- Authority a written response". The last day is the 14th day after (ILA s 44 excludes the day of the event).
GIVEN `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`ss 32(3), 42(2) -- the last day to respond` `the day` MEANS `the date` 14 `days after` `the day`

-- s 67(2): the documents must be available "during the period of 6 years after the licence ceases to be in force".
GIVEN `the day it ceased` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 67(2) -- the last day the documents must be available` `the day it ceased` MEANS `the date` 6 `years after` `the day it ceased`

-- s 67(4): a notice to produce "must state ... a time for complying with the notice, being not less than 14 days from the date
-- of the notice".
GIVEN `the date of the notice` IS A DATE, `the day to comply` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 67(4) -- the notice gives at least 14 days` `the date of the notice` `the day to comply` IF
    `the days from` `the date of the notice` `to` `the day to comply` AT LEAST 14

§§ `Duties with deadlines`

DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the licence holder`
    `the client`

DECLARE `What is done` IS ONE OF
    `give the Authority the annual information`
    `notify the Authority of the change`
    `notify the Authority of the suspected avoidance arrangement`

DECLARE `What became of the duty` IS ONE OF
    `done in time`
    `not done in time`
    `still open`

-- s 34(1), (3)(a): it is a condition of the licence that the holder provide the information within 28 days of the start of
-- the reporting period; s 36 makes complying with conditions a civil penalty provision (200 / 800 penalty units, s 94 item 6).
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `What is done`
`s 34 -- give the annual information` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the licence holder`
    MUST `give the Authority the annual information`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the licence holder` BECAUSE "the annual information was not given within 28 days of the start of the reporting period, a condition of the licence (s 34(1), (3)); a contravention of s 36"

-- s 43: "The holder of a licence must notify the Authority of any changes in the information provided to the Authority under
-- this Part within 30 days of the change." s 44(1): the same for prescribed changes.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `What is done`
`ss 43, 44 -- notify the change` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the licence holder`
    MUST `notify the Authority of the change`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the licence holder` BECAUSE "the change was not notified to the Authority within 30 days of the change (s 43, s 44(1))"

-- s 16(3): "The client must notify the Authority as soon as reasonably practicable after the client becomes aware, or
-- reasonably suspects, that the proposed arrangement is for the purpose of avoiding or circumventing an obligation". "As
-- soon as reasonably practicable" is a judgment: the number of days that was reasonably practicable is a fact given.
GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `What is done`
`s 16(3) -- notify the Authority of the avoidance arrangement` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the client`
    MUST `notify the Authority of the suspected avoidance arrangement`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the client` BECAUSE "the Authority was not notified as soon as reasonably practicable after the client became aware, or reasonably suspected, that the arrangement was for avoidance (s 16(3))"

-- The helper that runs a duty over what happened (in the shape of the Coroners Act 2008 encoding's helper). On the stable
-- l4 a CONSIDER on an EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH: where the act was done, FULFILLED means in time and
-- anything else late; where it was not, the helper asks whether doing it now would still be in time. It takes a DEONTIC
-- value, so it is never exported.
GIVEN `the rule`                  IS A DEONTIC `Party` `What is done`
      `the party`                 IS A `Party`
      `the act`                   IS A `What is done`
      `the act has been done`     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the time the act was done` IS A NUMBER
      `the time now`              IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`what became of` `the rule` `by` `the party` `doing` `the act` `the act has been done` `the time the act was done` `the time now` MEANS
    IF `the act has been done`
    THEN CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time the act was done`), (EVENT `the party` `the act` `the time the act was done`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `done in time`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`
    ELSE CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time now`), (EVENT `the party` `the act` `the time now`))
         WHEN FULFILLED THEN `still open`
         OTHERWISE `not done in time`

-- s 34 by dates.
GIVEN `the first day in force` IS A DATE, n IS A NUMBER, `it has been given` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day it was given` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`s 34 -- what became of the annual information` `the first day in force` n `it has been given` `the day it was given` `today` MEANS
    `what became of` (`s 34 -- give the annual information` 28) `by` `the licence holder` `doing` `give the Authority the annual information` `it has been given` (`the days from` `the start` `to` `the day it was given`) (`the days from` `the start` `to` `today`)
    WHERE
        `the start` MEANS `s 34(5) -- the start of reporting period` `the first day in force` n

-- ss 43, 44 by dates.
GIVEN `the day of the change` IS A DATE, `it has been notified` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day it was notified` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`ss 43, 44 -- what became of the notice of the change` `the day of the change` `it has been notified` `the day it was notified` `today` MEANS
    `what became of` (`ss 43, 44 -- notify the change` 30) `by` `the licence holder` `doing` `notify the Authority of the change` `it has been notified` (`the days from` `the day of the change` `to` `the day it was notified`) (`the days from` `the day of the change` `to` `today`)

-- s 16(3) by dates.
GIVEN `the day I became aware` IS A DATE, `the days reasonably practicable` IS A NUMBER, `it has been notified` IS A BOOLEAN, `the day it was notified` IS A DATE, `today` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `What became of the duty`
`s 16(3) -- what became of the notice of avoidance` `the day I became aware` `the days reasonably practicable` `it has been notified` `the day it was notified` `today` MEANS
    `what became of` (`s 16(3) -- notify the Authority of the avoidance arrangement` `the days reasonably practicable`) `by` `the client` `doing` `notify the Authority of the suspected avoidance arrangement` `it has been notified` (`the days from` `the day I became aware` `to` `the day it was notified`) (`the days from` `the day I became aware` `to` `today`)

§§ `Part 5 -- producing the licence, and self-incrimination`

-- s 46: "The holder of a licence must produce the licence for inspection upon request by any of the following (a) an
-- inspector; (b) a provider, a worker for a provider or a host; (c) a police officer; (d) a prescribed person." 12 penalty
-- units for a natural person, 60 for a body corporate.
DECLARE `Who asked` IS ONE OF
    `an inspector`
    `a provider`
    `a worker for a provider`
    `a host`
    `a police officer`
    `a person prescribed by the regulations`
    `someone else`
    `nobody has asked`

GIVEN `the person asking` IS A `Who asked`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 46 -- the licence must be produced` `the person asking` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the person asking`
    WHEN `someone else` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 46 lists who may ask and does not close the list with "only"; the Act says nothing of others)
    WHEN `nobody has asked` THEN JUST FALSE -- the duty arises "upon request" (fork F7)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 91: "(1) It is a reasonable excuse for a natural person to refuse or fail to give information, or do any other thing that
-- the person is required to do, under this Part if the giving of the information or the doing of the thing would tend to
-- incriminate the person. (2) Despite subsection (1), it is not a reasonable excuse for a natural person to refuse or fail to
-- produce a document". s 67A(4) says the same for a notice to produce or give information.
DECLARE `What I am required to do` IS ONE OF
    `give information or answer questions`
    `produce a document`
    `do another thing under Part 5`

GIVEN `I am a natural person` IS A BOOLEAN, `the requirement` IS A `What I am required to do`, `it would tend to incriminate me` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 91 -- self-incrimination is a reasonable excuse` `I am a natural person` `the requirement` `it would tend to incriminate me` MEANS
    IF NOT `I am a natural person`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 91 speaks only of a natural person)
    ELSE IF NOT `it would tend to incriminate me`
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 91 gives the excuse only where it would tend to incriminate; other excuses are not answered)
         ELSE CONSIDER `the requirement`
              WHEN `produce a document` THEN JUST FALSE
              OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `s 86 -- threats and detriment`

DECLARE `What was done to me` IS ONE OF
    `I was threatened or intimidated`
    `I was refused employment, hire or engagement`
    `I was dismissed, or my employment, hiring or engagement was terminated`
    `I was subjected to another detriment`
    `nothing of that kind`

DECLARE `Why it was done` IS ONE OF
    `because of information under the Act that I gave or intended to give, or to stop me giving it`
    `because of a process under the Act I took part in or intended to take part in, or to stop me continuing it`
    `because of a requirement under the Act I complied with or intended to comply with, or to stop me complying`
    `for another reason`

-- s 86(1): "A person must not, by threat or intimidation, persuade or attempt to persuade another person (a) not to provide
-- information under this Act; or (b) not to continue with any process under this Act; or (c) not to comply with any other
-- requirement under this Act." (2): "A person must not refuse to employ, hire or engage, or dismiss or terminate the
-- employment, hiring or engagement of, another person or subject another person to any detriment because the other person
-- (a) intends to provide, provides or has provided information under this Act; or (b) ... takes part in ... any process
-- under this Act; or (c) ... complies ... with any other requirement under this Act." Civil penalty provisions (200 / 800).
GIVEN `the treatment` IS A `What was done to me`, `the reason` IS A `Why it was done`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 86 -- what was done is forbidden` `the treatment` `the reason` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the reason`
    WHEN `for another reason` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 86 forbids only conduct for the reasons it names)
    OTHERWISE CONSIDER `the treatment`
              WHEN `nothing of that kind` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording: s 86 forbids only the conduct it names)
              OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

§§ `Penalties and proceedings`

DECLARE `Provision contravened` IS ONE OF
    `s 13 providing labour hire services without a licence`
    `s 14 advertising labour hire services without a licence`
    `s 15(1) entering into an arrangement with an unlicensed provider`
    `s 16(2) entering into an avoidance arrangement`
    `s 16(3) not reporting an avoidance arrangement`
    `s 36 not complying with a licence condition`
    `s 37(3) not complying with a notice to comply`
    `s 43 not notifying changes`
    `s 44(1) not notifying prescribed changes`
    `s 45 not ensuring nominated officers are available`
    `s 67(1) not keeping documents available for inspection`
    `s 67(2) not keeping documents available for 6 years after the licence ends`
    `s 86(1) threats or intimidation`
    `s 86(2) dismissal or detriment`
    `s 46 not producing the licence (offence)`
    `s 67(5) not complying with a notice to produce documents (offence)`
    `s 67A(5) not complying with a direction to produce or give information (offence)`
    `s 74(2) not complying with an inspector's requirement on entry (offence)`
    `s 79(2) dealing with a thing under an embargo notice (offence)`
    `s 84(2) not assisting an inspector executing a warrant (offence)`
    `s 85(2) not allowing a person assisting an inspector access (offence)`
    `s 87 giving false or misleading information or documents (offence)`
    `s 88(1) hindering or obstructing an inspector or the Commissioner (offence)`
    `s 88(2) assaulting, intimidating or threatening an inspector or the Commissioner (offence)`

-- s 94(2) table (civil penalty provisions) and the penalties written under each offence. Penalty units; a penalty unit's
-- value is fixed each year under the Monetary Units Act 2004 (not deposited).
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision contravened`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 94 -- a civil penalty provision` `the provision` IF
    CONSIDER `the provision`
    WHEN `s 46 not producing the licence (offence)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 67(5) not complying with a notice to produce documents (offence)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 67A(5) not complying with a direction to produce or give information (offence)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 74(2) not complying with an inspector's requirement on entry (offence)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 79(2) dealing with a thing under an embargo notice (offence)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 84(2) not assisting an inspector executing a warrant (offence)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 85(2) not allowing a person assisting an inspector access (offence)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 87 giving false or misleading information or documents (offence)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 88(1) hindering or obstructing an inspector or the Commissioner (offence)` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `s 88(2) assaulting, intimidating or threatening an inspector or the Commissioner (offence)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision contravened`, `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum penalty units for` `the provision` `a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `a body corporate` THEN `the body corporate's` ELSE `the natural person's`
    WHERE
        `the natural person's` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the provision`
            WHEN `s 13 providing labour hire services without a licence` THEN 800
            WHEN `s 14 advertising labour hire services without a licence` THEN 200
            WHEN `s 15(1) entering into an arrangement with an unlicensed provider` THEN 800
            WHEN `s 16(2) entering into an avoidance arrangement` THEN 800
            WHEN `s 16(3) not reporting an avoidance arrangement` THEN 200
            WHEN `s 36 not complying with a licence condition` THEN 200
            WHEN `s 37(3) not complying with a notice to comply` THEN 200
            WHEN `s 43 not notifying changes` THEN 40
            WHEN `s 44(1) not notifying prescribed changes` THEN 800
            WHEN `s 45 not ensuring nominated officers are available` THEN 40
            WHEN `s 67(1) not keeping documents available for inspection` THEN 200
            WHEN `s 67(2) not keeping documents available for 6 years after the licence ends` THEN 200
            WHEN `s 86(1) threats or intimidation` THEN 200
            WHEN `s 86(2) dismissal or detriment` THEN 200
            WHEN `s 46 not producing the licence (offence)` THEN 12
            WHEN `s 67(5) not complying with a notice to produce documents (offence)` THEN 150
            WHEN `s 67A(5) not complying with a direction to produce or give information (offence)` THEN 150
            WHEN `s 74(2) not complying with an inspector's requirement on entry (offence)` THEN 150
            WHEN `s 79(2) dealing with a thing under an embargo notice (offence)` THEN 150
            WHEN `s 84(2) not assisting an inspector executing a warrant (offence)` THEN 150
            WHEN `s 85(2) not allowing a person assisting an inspector access (offence)` THEN 75
            WHEN `s 87 giving false or misleading information or documents (offence)` THEN 150
            WHEN `s 88(1) hindering or obstructing an inspector or the Commissioner (offence)` THEN 75
            WHEN `s 88(2) assaulting, intimidating or threatening an inspector or the Commissioner (offence)` THEN 240
        `the body corporate's` MEANS
            CONSIDER `the provision`
            WHEN `s 13 providing labour hire services without a licence` THEN 3200
            WHEN `s 14 advertising labour hire services without a licence` THEN 800
            WHEN `s 15(1) entering into an arrangement with an unlicensed provider` THEN 3200
            WHEN `s 16(2) entering into an avoidance arrangement` THEN 3200
            WHEN `s 16(3) not reporting an avoidance arrangement` THEN 800
            WHEN `s 36 not complying with a licence condition` THEN 800
            WHEN `s 37(3) not complying with a notice to comply` THEN 800
            WHEN `s 43 not notifying changes` THEN 160
            WHEN `s 44(1) not notifying prescribed changes` THEN 3200
            WHEN `s 45 not ensuring nominated officers are available` THEN 160
            WHEN `s 67(1) not keeping documents available for inspection` THEN 800
            WHEN `s 67(2) not keeping documents available for 6 years after the licence ends` THEN 800
            WHEN `s 86(1) threats or intimidation` THEN 800
            WHEN `s 86(2) dismissal or detriment` THEN 800
            WHEN `s 46 not producing the licence (offence)` THEN 60
            WHEN `s 67(5) not complying with a notice to produce documents (offence)` THEN 750
            WHEN `s 67A(5) not complying with a direction to produce or give information (offence)` THEN 750
            WHEN `s 74(2) not complying with an inspector's requirement on entry (offence)` THEN 750
            WHEN `s 79(2) dealing with a thing under an embargo notice (offence)` THEN 750
            WHEN `s 84(2) not assisting an inspector executing a warrant (offence)` THEN 750
            WHEN `s 85(2) not allowing a person assisting an inspector access (offence)` THEN 375
            WHEN `s 87 giving false or misleading information or documents (offence)` THEN 750
            WHEN `s 88(1) hindering or obstructing an inspector or the Commissioner (offence)` THEN 375
            WHEN `s 88(2) assaulting, intimidating or threatening an inspector or the Commissioner (offence)` THEN 1200

-- s 88(2): "In the case of a natural person, 240 penalty units or imprisonment for 2 years or both". No other offence in the
-- Act carries imprisonment.
GIVEN `the provision` IS A `Provision contravened`, `a body corporate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum years of imprisonment for` `the provision` `a body corporate` MEANS
    IF `a body corporate`
    THEN 0
    ELSE CONSIDER `the provision`
         WHEN `s 88(2) assaulting, intimidating or threatening an inspector or the Commissioner (offence)` THEN 2
         OTHERWISE 0

DECLARE `Whether a pecuniary penalty can be ordered` IS ONE OF
    `yes, by the Magistrates' Court or the Supreme Court (s 93(6)(a))`
    `yes, by the Supreme Court only (s 93(6)(b))`
    `no: the application was not made within 6 years of the contravention (s 93(7))`
    `no: you have been convicted of an offence for substantially the same conduct (s 97)`
    `not while the criminal proceedings for substantially the same conduct go on: the civil proceedings are stayed (s 98(1))`
    `not under Part 6: the provision is an offence, not a civil penalty provision`

-- s 93(2)(a), (6), (7), ss 97, 98. "within 6 years of the contravention": the last day is the sixth anniversary (fork F8).
GIVEN `the provision`                        IS A `Provision contravened`
      `a body corporate`                     IS A BOOLEAN
      `the day of the contravention`         IS A DATE
      `the day of the application`           IS A DATE
      `convicted for substantially the same conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `criminal proceedings are pending`     IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Whether a pecuniary penalty can be ordered`
`Part 6 -- whether a pecuniary penalty can be ordered` `the provision` `a body corporate` `the day of the contravention` `the day of the application` `convicted for substantially the same conduct` `criminal proceedings are pending` MEANS
    IF NOT `s 94 -- a civil penalty provision` `the provision`
    THEN `not under Part 6: the provision is an offence, not a civil penalty provision`
    ELSE IF (`the date` 6 `years after` `the day of the contravention`) `is before` `the day of the application`
         THEN `no: the application was not made within 6 years of the contravention (s 93(7))`
         ELSE IF `convicted for substantially the same conduct`
              THEN `no: you have been convicted of an offence for substantially the same conduct (s 97)`
              ELSE IF `criminal proceedings are pending`
                   THEN `not while the criminal proceedings for substantially the same conduct go on: the civil proceedings are stayed (s 98(1))`
                   ELSE IF (`a body corporate` AND (`the maximum penalty units for` `the provision` TRUE AT MOST 2500)) OR ((NOT `a body corporate`) AND (`the maximum penalty units for` `the provision` FALSE AT MOST 500))
                        THEN `yes, by the Magistrates' Court or the Supreme Court (s 93(6)(a))`
                        ELSE `yes, by the Supreme Court only (s 93(6)(b))`

-- s 105: "proceedings for an offence against this Act may be commenced within 6 years after the date on which the offence is
-- alleged to have been committed" (fork F8).
GIVEN `the day of the offence` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 105 -- the last day to commence a prosecution` `the day of the offence` MEANS `the date` 6 `years after` `the day of the offence`

-- s 93(7) as a date.
GIVEN `the day of the contravention` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 93(7) -- the last day to apply for a pecuniary penalty` `the day of the contravention` MEANS `the date` 6 `years after` `the day of the contravention`

§§ `s 102 -- review by VCAT`

DECLARE `The decision` IS ONE OF
    `a decision to grant a licence (s 24)`
    `a decision to refuse to grant a licence (s 24)`
    `a decision to renew a licence (s 29)`
    `a decision to refuse to renew a licence (s 29)`
    `a decision to impose a condition on a licence (s 33)`
    `a decision to issue a notice to comply (s 37)`
    `a decision to vary a licence (s 38)`
    `a decision to refuse my application to vary a licence (s 38)`
    `a decision to suspend a licence (s 39)`
    `a decision to cancel a licence (s 40)`
    `another decision`

DECLARE `My part in it` IS ONE OF
    `the applicant for the licence or its renewal`
    `the holder of the licence`
    `an interested person who objected to the application`
    `someone else`

-- s 102(1) lists the decisions; (2) "eligible applicant means (a) in the case of a decision relating to an application for a
-- licence or renewal of a licence, the applicant ... or an interested person who made an objection to the application; and
-- (b) in the case of any other decision relating to a licence, the holder of the licence." A "means" definition: someone
-- outside it is not eligible (JUST FALSE). A decision not listed: NOTHING (fork F9 for a refusal to vary).
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `The decision`, `my part` IS A `My part in it`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102 -- I may apply to VCAT for review` `the decision` `my part` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `a decision to grant a licence (s 24)` THEN `as applicant or objector`
    WHEN `a decision to refuse to grant a licence (s 24)` THEN `as applicant or objector`
    WHEN `a decision to renew a licence (s 29)` THEN `as applicant or objector`
    WHEN `a decision to refuse to renew a licence (s 29)` THEN `as applicant or objector`
    WHEN `a decision to refuse my application to vary a licence (s 38)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 102(1)(g) lists "a decision to vary a licence" only, though s 38(7)(b) says the notice of a refusal must state the holder may apply to VCAT; fork F9, finding 5)
    WHEN `another decision` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent: s 102 lists the decisions it reaches; other review rights are outside the Act)
    OTHERWISE `as holder`
    WHERE
        `as applicant or objector` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my part`
            WHEN `the applicant for the licence or its renewal` THEN JUST TRUE
            WHEN `an interested person who objected to the application` THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE
        `as holder` MEANS
            CONSIDER `my part`
            WHEN `the holder of the licence` THEN JUST TRUE
            OTHERWISE JUST FALSE

-- s 102(1): "within 28 days of being notified of the decision".
GIVEN `the day I was notified` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 102 -- the last day to apply to VCAT` `the day I was notified` MEANS `the date` 28 `days after` `the day I was notified`
